 # luci-app-sms-manager
 Simple user interface to handle SMS / USSD / AT commands via ModemManager application.
 
+## ModemManager integration in this checkout
+
+This checkout is pinned to upstream commit `322392909e046c172f06e8dfff8a956b9ede4bbb`,
+the current `main` tip after the `1.0.9-r20260225` release. SMS listing, reading,
+deletion and sending use `/usr/bin/mmcli` and ModemManager's D-Bus API. The status
+overview also reads modem data through `mmcli -J`, so the package does not require
+the separate `modemdata` or `sms-tool` packages.
+
+The optional AT page still sends commands through `mmcli --command`; it does not
+open a modem device node. ModemManager must be built with
+`CONFIG_MODEMMANAGER_WITH_AT_COMMAND_VIA_DBUS=y` for that page to work. SMS itself
+does not require that optional build flag.
+
+The local package release is 20260906. Its init entry registers procd reload
+triggers but starts no worker with the default lednotify=0 configuration.
+Notifications and mail forwarding require an explicit user action; mailsend is
+declared as a dependency. SMS text is passed via a private temporary UTF-8 file,
+and mutations require write access. See tests/test-sms-manager.py for the mocked
+text/permissions/failure checks; no real SMS is sent by those tests.
+
